:Chili Powder|chili powder]]\n* 1 ½ tbsp [[Cookbook:Cayenne Pepper|cayenne pepper]]\n* 2 tbsp [[Cookbook:Lemon Pepper|lemon pepper]]\n* 2 tbsp [[Cookbook:Garlic Powder|garlic powder]]\n* 1 tbsp [[Cookbook:Salt|salt]]\n* 1 tbsp black [[Cookbook:Pepper|peppercorns]], cracked\n* Forearm-sized mesquite wood chunks\n* Yellow [[Cookbook:Mustard|mustard]]\n\n== Procedure ==\n#Combine seasonings. Set aside.\n#[[Cookbook:Brush|Brush]] chicken with mustard. This will help make a crust. Press seasoning mixture into both sides of meat. Refrigerate 30 minutes.\n#Preheat smoker to 225°F with mesquite. Add chicken pieces and insert a probe [[Cookbook:Thermometer|thermometer]] into one of them. Cook, adding wood as needed, until internal temperature reaches 170°F.\n#Move to a very very high [[Cookbook:Grill|grill]] and cook until charred and marked. Flip and repeat.\n#Serve immediately with desired side dishes.\n\n[[Category:Recipes using chicken]]\n[[Category:Recipes using garlic powder]]\n[[Category:Smoked recipes]]\n[[Category:Main course recipes]]\n[[Category:Recipes using chili powder]]\n[[Category:Recipes using cayenne]]\n[[Category:Recipes using salt]]\n[[Category:Recipes using pepper]]\n[[Category:Recipes using yellow mustard]]\n[[Category:Recipes using lemon pepper]]","isRecipe":true,"recipe":{"name":"Smoked Garlic Chicken","nameAr":null,"servings":null,"servingsSourceText":null,"ingredients":[{"id":"source-line-1","name":"4 whole chicken leg quarters, skin removed","sourceText":"4 whole chicken leg quarters, skin removed","amountText":"4 whole chicken leg quarters, skin removed","amount":null,"unit":null,"foodBinding":null},{"id":"source-line-2","name":"¼ cup paprika","sourceText":"¼ cup paprika","amountText":"¼ cup paprika","amount":null,"unit":null,"foodBinding":null},{"id":"source-line-3","name":"2 tbsp chili powder","sourceText":"2 tbsp chili powder","amountText":"2 tbsp chili powder","amount":null,"unit":null,"foodBinding":null},{"id":"source-line-4","name":"1 ½ tbsp